A||N||10||grinthock||Where did you install your alarm box?||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||05-31-2001||04:59 PM||||Ok this is gonan be hard to ask!  I know people do'nt like to devulge this, but where is the best place to put your alarm control box?  I want to put it somewhere that is hidden away yet accessible if I need to service the unit... ideas?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://grinthock.2y.net/pics/87gt/S_P000386.JPG">  <P>Home page: <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com<BR>Home" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroworld.com<BR>Home</A>  of the fiero voting booth!<BR>Owner of 85 GT<BR>87 GT Silver<BR>1995 Ford Escort Wagoon POS||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jay||05-31-2001||05:07 PM||||Do you mean the Brain?  Best place is uder or in your dash.  Rarely have to get access to it.  I don't mind divulging that because several things have to be done in sequence before my car will start.  Including the Ignited push button starter and viper alarm.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kick.gif">  <BR>THE NORTHSTAR GIVES YOU A REAL KICK IN THE ASS!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||05-31-2001||05:21 PM||||I had mine professionally installed but I picked where it was installed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Sensors on each side down by the door trim by your feet..  box up above the cd player (pull off front case surrounding radio to view..<P>alarm button (flashing light) was drilled through the front case above the cd player..<P>Valet switch was drilled into the plastic case under the steering wheel..<P>The speaker was put up beside the horn (on the outside of the front trunk)<P>Works great..nice and loud and if anyone touches either side..it lets everyone know  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>plus the flashing light above the stereo makes thieves think twice  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||05-31-2001||05:27 PM||||Hmm that's a nice place behind the radio!  For sure!  but alas, I have a din 1.5 radio.. not really enough room.  But that radio is coming out this weekend anyway.... Sold it for a 1 Din unit||||reg||1
Z||000004||coyote||05-31-2001||06:23 PM||||When i did my 87, i placed under the carpet on the passanger side. Located just under the radio pod is a preformed area for the factory sub woofer amp. worked out great, you cant tell it is even there.<P><BR>Coyote||||reg||1
Z||000005||drednot||05-31-2001||07:03 PM||||Come on, It's a Fiero!  No one is going to steel it!  It can't be worth more than $4000||||reg||10
Z||000006||KRMFiero||05-31-2001||07:14 PM||||I installed my box by the chime box in the pasanger compartment,  and i put the sierin that came with it in the front trunk and i bought anouther on and put it in the engine compartment so if someone brakes and and cuts the wieres to one siren they will have to find the other one also<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||05-31-2001||08:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by drednot:<BR><B>Come on, It's a Fiero!  No one is going to steel it!  It can't be worth more than $4000</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No, it's the $10,000 worth of stereo equipment were protecting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>The 3 best locations to install the brain box are:<BR>1. If not equipped with factory subwoofer (performance sound) on the passenger side under the carpet of the console is a small pocket where the stock amp would sit. (this is only valid on 86 thru 88 cars)<P>2. Remove the top of the dash and there is a pocket of space between the defroster vent and the fire wall.<P>3. What ever location is hard for you to access. If it is hard for you it's hard for a thief to locate. Under the driver side dash is the first place a thief looks. Most thieves already have a jumper wire made to by-pass the alarm. If it takes more than 30 seconds and they can't dis-able the alarm, they usually leave. <BR>The purpose of the alarm is to keep the non-professional thieves out. If a pro wants it it's gone.<BR>(short of the James Bond method of using high explosives!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   )<P>Usually an alarm will keep the punks from breaking in just to trash the car or snag the radio/stereo stuff.<P>Mine is well hidden and a real pain to get at. Finally, I would recommend installing it yourself and soldering the wires. Using clips and such like the alarm dealers, can cause problems over time. I have installed many alarms into many types of cars. Never had one go bad yet. One car is 11 years old and the alarm still works great.<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000008||grinthock||05-31-2001||08:57 PM||||I will be doing it myself, and I ALWAYS solder them (no cold solder joints!).  That seems like a good spot I will have to check it out.... I will be putting in a backup battery so that if the battery is cut the system will still whail (none of these cheap 9V battery backups)....  The backup will be hidden too, (I have a electronics shop here that sells some nice 12V batteries||||reg||1
Z||000009||Songman||06-01-2001||09:55 PM||||The one in my T-top is under the speaker on the driver's side of the dash. It was already installed when I got the car. The reason I know this is because there is no speaker and I can see it laying there! hehe<BR>Those of you who have seen it know that I still haven't put it together yet! hehe<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||12
Z||000010||Mach10||06-02-2001||04:22 AM||||Who needs an alarm? Just jam a Shock-Taser into the seat cushion, and relay it up to a timer and door switch. Anyone sitting down within 20 seconds of opening the door is in for a nasty shock...<P>Actually, here are some more doable security solutions:<P>1) For stereos, epoxy a LARGE number of small gauge BARBED fishhooks under the dash, and around the stereo components. Much better than razors.<BR>2) Wire an electrical fire-extinguisher to an auxillary port on your alarm, and modify it to flood the passenger compartment with your choice of:<BR>-Halon (default. Not a good thing to breath for long. It's like holding your breath)<BR>-Mace<BR>-Pepper Spray<BR>-CS Teargas<BR>-Hydrogen Sulfide<BR>-Skunk Oil<BR>-Ether<BR>-NO2<BR>-Plain CO2+Water... Can't steal if you can't see...<BR>3) For the larger stereos, put strips of Al foil around the equipment, and ground it. Hard-wire your stiffening cap to the battery, and run in parrallel to a Tesla coil, and run leads to OTHER bits of foil placed NEAR to the grounded ones. Anything getting between the two is in for a nasty surprise (fingers, mice, dust etc)<BR>4)use a spare ignition coil, and "miswire" your power locks. Make sure to build yourself an INSULATED key<BR>5)Buy lexan glass replacements, redo locks a-la-childproof, and have the entire electrical system rewired for a "lockdown" if the alarm is activated. Easy to break INTO The car? Maybe. Guarantee it'll be harder breaking out...<BR>6)Do what I'm doing: Have a switch panel controlling fuel, start, etc. Build in a keypad. Use TONS of like-colored wiring behind the panel. Anyone rips it apart trying to bypass it will be in for an electrical engineer's nightmare   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>7) Run a separate coil  and get it to fire like the active one. Have the main lead go to a spot directly under the seat, where you were SURE to put a HV probe, and thread grouded copper wire through the seat fabric. Have a hidden OFF switch for this.<BR>8)Wire the alarm up to activate your extreme stereo. Nothing like AquaGen's "Phat Bass" at 3 in the morning to arouse suspicion. Include horn, as well as normal siren.<P>Any others?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 06-02-2001).]||||reg||1
